## Role Definitions

### Owner
- Ultimate decision authority for the project
- Responsible for project vision and direction
- Has final say on all disputes
- Can delegate authority to other maintainers

### Safety Officer
- Responsible for safety-critical decisions
- Has veto authority over any change that affects safety
- Must approve all changes to canAdvance(), canActivate(), review states
- Can halt any operation that violates safety principles

### Lead Maintainer
- Day-to-day management of the project
- Reviews and merges pull requests
- Maintains release schedule
- Coordinates with contributors

## Contact

For security issues, please contact the safety officer privately.
For general issues, please use GitHub Issues.
For design discussions, please use GitHub Discussions.

## Becoming a Maintainer

To become a maintainer:

1. Contribute significantly to the project (code, documentation, review)
2. Demonstrate understanding of the safety principles
3. Be nominated by an existing maintainer
4. Be approved by the owner
5. Sign the maintainer agreement (if applicable)

